WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.000
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.454
Yeah.

00:00:11.454 --> 00:00:12.354
[BLEEP]

00:00:12.354 --> 00:00:13.830
[CHUCKLING]

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.610
From here, it's hard
to tell the scale.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:16.710
Yeah, it's so--

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:19.710
it's so big.

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:24.430
WILL GADD: If you aren't scared
walking into Helmcken Falls,

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.140
something is wrong with you.

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.190
Imagine a covered
sports stadium.

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:32.450
And you cut it in half.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:36.290
And coming out of the
ceiling, there's a waterfall.

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:39.710
And it hits the ground, sprays
all over everything behind it.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:45.700
At the bottom, there's this
giant caldron out of ice.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:47.990
We called it the
caldron of doom.

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:49.720
And if you went into
the caldron of doom,

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:51.300
they aren't ever
going to find you.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:57.580
SARAH HUENIKEN: There's this
huge cliff with thousands

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:01.645
of big hanging icicles.

00:01:01.645 --> 00:01:03.460
These are falling.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:06.945
It's an ever
changing environment.

00:01:06.945 --> 00:01:11.660
WILL GADD: You have freezing
mist on you continually.

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:13.220
It's the most
complicated environment

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:14.825
I've ever been in in my life.

00:01:17.954 --> 00:01:23.660
MAN: Helmcken Falls is
outrageously difficult.

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:27.560
Just the physical act
of climbing in that kind

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:31.550
of terrain, it's akin to
doing hundreds of pull-ups,

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.730
but also doing a
highly choreographed

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:36.155
ballet at the same time.

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:44.155
No one's ever tried or climbed
a route of this scale before.

00:01:47.755 --> 00:01:49.930
WILL GADD: The first time
I went to Helmcken Falls,

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:52.150
I saw this line.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:53.860
But it was probably
about 10 years

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:57.370
of climbing all over the
world and a half dozen

00:01:57.370 --> 00:02:02.230
other trips to Helmcken
to make that climb happen.

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:05.140
The idea was to do a line
from the bottom of the falls

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:07.990
to the top of the
falls, take the path of,

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:13.240
like, steepest
maximum resistance.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:15.550
And I wanted it to be
kind of the culmination

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:17.770
of my ice and mixed career.

00:02:23.758 --> 00:02:26.780
MAN: The hammer and
the ratchet I just

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:30.791
put on the sternal
attachment to the harness.

00:02:30.791 --> 00:02:32.900
MAN: To do a first
ascent on something

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:35.810
like Helmcken Falls
requires a ton of work

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:38.210
because you have to
establish the route.

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:40.250
You have to equip
the route, which

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:45.320
means you need to find it,
then put in bolts for where

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:47.520
he can clip in the rope.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.740
This is a massive undertaking.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:52.720
It can take weeks.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:56.430
The other aspect is that it's
in a dynamic environment.

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:00.450
Temperature and weather have
a lot of impact on the route.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:06.540
So Will is racing against time
because as the season warms up,

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:09.831
the route might
not be climbable.

00:03:09.831 --> 00:03:11.800
WILL GADD: We've
got two teams of two

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:14.533
working full time
to get it done.

00:03:14.533 --> 00:03:16.450
SARAH HUENIKEN: Yeah,
that hold feels sketchy.

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:18.820
Yeah, you got to get
your pick in right.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:23.260
SARAH HUENIKEN: [GRUNTING]
Any trip you do with Will

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:25.045
is kind of a once in
a lifetime chance.

00:03:25.045 --> 00:03:27.150
Let's make as much
progress as we can.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:31.010
Like, if you're not
psyched to go up, I will.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:34.150
But I also know that it
can be very dangerous.

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:37.070
And there's a lot of
things we don't control.

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:42.280
And that can be hard to be
his partner-partner in life

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:45.340
and his climbing partner.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:47.710
But leading up to
it, I saw everything

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:50.800
he did to be ready to climb.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:54.150
[MUSIC PLAYING]

